# =============================================================================
# opcgw — environment configuration
#
# This is the SINGLE place that holds the gateway's environment configuration.
# docker-compose.yml loads it via `env_file: .env`, so every variable defined
# here is passed to the container; nothing is set in the compose file itself.
#
# Setup:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit .env and set the REQUIRED values below
#   chmod 600 .env
#   docker compose up
#
# `.env` is git-ignored; this `.env.example` ships placeholders only and is
# safe to commit.
#
# Every variable uses the OPCGW_ prefix; `__` (double underscore) separates
# nested configuration keys.
#
# ⚠️ Since v2.8.0 (Story J-2 / #169) env overrides are RESTRICTED to an
# allowlist: the web Admin page (SQLite-backed) is authoritative for the
# editable configuration, and a non-allowlisted OPCGW_<SECTION>__<FIELD> var
# is IGNORED (with an `env_var_ignored` WARN naming it at boot). Env-capable:
# the two secrets (API token, OPC UA/web password), the web bootstrap trio
# (WEB__ENABLED / WEB__BIND_ADDRESS / WEB__PORT), OPCGW_OPCUA__HOST_PORT, the
# [logging]/[storage] sections, and the short-form knobs (OPCGW_LOG_DIR,
# OPCGW_LOG_LEVEL, budget/cap tuning). Everything else: use the Admin page.
# =============================================================================

# --- SECRETS (optional — the first-run web wizard can collect these) ---------
#
# Story F-2: the ChirpStack API token and the OPC UA password can be supplied
# through the browser at http://<host>:<port>/setup on first boot (it writes
# them to config/secrets.toml, file mode 0600). Set them here ONLY if you want
# to skip the wizard / provision unattended. Leave them commented out to use
# the zero-touch wizard.
#
# NOTE on the web-UI login: opcgw's web UI reuses the OPC UA credential
# ([opcua].user_name + user_password) for HTTP Basic auth — there is no
# separate admin account. So OPCGW_OPCUA__USER_PASSWORD below IS the web-UI
# login password; when you leave it commented out, the wizard sets it. The
# log-file location (OPCGW_LOG_DIR, below) stays exclusively in this file.
# Since v2.8.0 the user NAME is Admin-page-managed ([opcua].user_name):
# an OPCGW_OPCUA__USER_NAME env var is IGNORED.

# ChirpStack API token. Must have permission to list applications/devices,
# read metrics, and access the configured tenant.
#OPCGW_CHIRPSTACK__API_TOKEN=replace-with-your-chirpstack-api-token

# OPC UA / Web UI password. Paired with the user name below; also used for the
# web UI's HTTP Basic auth. Choose a strong value.
#OPCGW_OPCUA__USER_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-strong-password

# --- COMMON (uncomment to override the built-in defaults) --------------------

# ChirpStack gRPC endpoint (host:port).
# ⚠️ IGNORED since v2.8.0 — set it on the web Admin page (or in the seed
# config.toml for the very first boot / the /setup wizard).
#OPCGW_CHIRPSTACK__SERVER_ADDRESS=chirpstack.example.com:8080

# OPC UA / Web UI user name. Default: opcua-user
# ⚠️ IGNORED since v2.8.0 — manage it on the web Admin page.
#OPCGW_OPCUA__USER_NAME=opcua-user

# OPC UA listen port. Default: 4840 (standard OPC UA port). If you change it,
# update the published port in docker-compose.yml to match.
#OPCGW_OPCUA__HOST_PORT=4840

# NOTE on the advertised endpoint host (issue #163): `[opcua].host_ip_address`
# is the host opcgw advertises in its endpoint/discovery URL AND (async-opcua
# 0.17) the address it binds. Manage it — and other opcua knobs like
# `max_keep_alive_count` — from the web Admin page (SQLite). Since v2.8.0 an
# `OPCGW_OPCUA__HOST_IP_ADDRESS` (or `MAX_KEEP_ALIVE_COUNT`, etc.) env var here
# is IGNORED (before v2.8.0 it silently OUTRANKED the web value — the #168
# shadow trap that caused SCADA connection churn by advertising `0.0.0.0`).
# In Docker use a resolvable name plus an `extra_hosts: ["<name>:0.0.0.0"]`
# entry in docker-compose.yml (see that file's comment and the manual).

# Enable the embedded web UI (first-run wizard + configuration). Default: true
#OPCGW_WEB__ENABLED=true

# Web UI port. Default: 8080. docker-compose.yml publishes this port.
#OPCGW_WEB__PORT=8080

# Log verbosity: error | warn | info | debug | trace. Default: info
#OPCGW_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Storage-latency WARN budgets (GH-144). These only tune when a slow SQLite
# query / batch is logged at warn vs debug — no functional effect. The defaults
# are sized for NAS / network-backed storage; lower them on fast local SSDs to
# restore early regression detection. Positive integer milliseconds.
# Storage-query budget. Default: 250
#OPCGW_STORAGE_QUERY_BUDGET_MS=250
# End-of-cycle batch-write budget. Default: 2000
#OPCGW_BATCH_WRITE_BUDGET_MS=2000
